// An unregistered `@name` in decorator position is rejected by NAME (E0003) — and only by name.
// Its argument is not a syntax error: the directive grammar was unified with `#[...]`'s, so
// `@openapi("petstore.yaml")` parses as a directive with one string argument. That is the seam a
// registered extension directive will slot into; today nothing registers the name.
//
// The help lists the decorator directives, generated from the directive set rather than written
// out, so it cannot list a directive that no longer exists or omit one that does.
// expect: error E0003 at 10:2
// expect: exit 1
@openapi("petstore.yaml")
struct Pet { name: string }
echo "unreached"
